# High-level term of the DLPNO-CCSD(T)/def2-TZVPP (+def2-TZVPP/C) : r2SCAN-3c
# composite correction, COMPUTATIONAL.md C8 (K + H2O2 -> KP, item 1).
#
# Species: the VERIFIED transition state, geometry ../verify_exact_hessian/job.xyz
# (exact NumFreq: one imaginary mode at -576.3 cm-1).
#
# Its 22-atom QM-region fragment could NOT be taken from the sibling
# geometry run: geometry_r2scan3c-xtb/ts/job.xyz was overwritten by a crashed
# OptTS attempt and ts/job.QMRegion.xyz belongs to that bad geometry
# (O136-C129 2.596 A). It was re-emitted for the verified geometry by the
# one-cycle opt in geometry_r2scan3c-xtb/ts/qmregion_extract/ (O136-C129
# 1.820 A, heaviest-atom mismatch 0.004 A) and copied here.
#
# Single point on that fragment ALONE; pairs with ../r2scan3c/job.inp:
#
#   G_final = G(r2SCAN-3c/xtb, full 140-atom system, 298.15 K)
#           + [ E(DLPNO-CCSD(T), fragment) - E(r2SCAN-3c, fragment) ]
#
# assembled by orca_io.composite_free_energy_eh. CPCM(Water) here, matching the
# register's convention for every isolated-species task (C1, C4-C6, C9); the
# geometry tier is ddCOSMO(Water) only because plain CPCM is not implemented
# for QM/XTB. Level and basis follow the ORCA 6.1 "accurate barriers" tutorial
# rather than trusting any single DFT functional for the final number.
# nprocs 8 / maxcore 4000: homelab-benchmarked; 8 physical P-cores beat 16/24
# ranks on this hybrid P/E chip for fragments this small.
! DLPNO-CCSD(T) def2-TZVPP def2-TZVPP/C CPCM(Water) TightSCF

%maxcore 4000

%pal
   nprocs 8
end

* xyzfile 0 1 job.xyz
